today we discussed two proposals to  strengthen the external borders and I'm  pleased to be able to announce today  that the council agreed that we have to  reinforce the checks at our external  borders so we adopted the measures and  the proposed changes in the code on that  issue we also continued our discussion  on European kosem border guard system  and we concluded that the agency should  serve three goals provide better  information about migration flows  identify the weak spots at our external  borders and respond swiftly to the  borders when they are at risk we have to  solve the migration crisis together  together with all Member States but also  together with all the countries along  the Balkan route and together with  Turkey and I understand that the high  influx puts countries under enormous  pressure and I also understand the urge  to take measures but those measures have  to be communicated and coordinated  better and we agreed today between all  the countries that from now on all  relevant countries have to be involved  on such matters measures are being taken  or further Titans in the next and days  we need tangible and clear results on  the ground otherwise there is a danger  that is a risk that the whole system  will completely break down the route  along the Western Balkans yes the  situation is very critical we have a  shared responsibility all of us towards  our neighboring states both EU and  non-eu but also towards those desperate  people we cannot continue with the wave  through policy the European Council was  crystal clear on that and we cannot put  caps or how many asylum seekers receive  this is simply not according to EU and  international rules to those who think  that we need national solutions because  a European approach is not working I say  it is precisely national actions that  are hindering a European approach
 

